{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed168776016/5/codegen_prompts/4.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/5`\n- 题号：`4`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed168776016/5/4.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"4\">\n- `description`：将网格中的多个形状按嵌套包含关系组装成俄罗斯套娃式的同心结构，最内层形状的颜色决定所有层的排列锚点。\n- `Input structure`：背景为 Black。网格上散布着若干个不同大小的单色实心矩形（不含 Black），矩形之间互不重叠、互不接触。这些矩形的宽度和高度各不相同，且恰好可以按面积从小到大排成严格递增序列。每个矩形的颜色互不相同。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 将所有矩形按面积从大到小排序。\n  2. 以最小矩形（面积最小者）的中心位置为锚点。\n  3. 在输出中，将所有矩形以该锚点为中心重新叠放：最大的矩形在最底层，最小的在最顶层，所有矩形共享同一中心点。\n  4. 叠放时大矩形先绘制、小矩形后绘制（即小矩形覆盖大矩形的中心部分），形成同心嵌套的彩色矩形环。\n  5. 输出网格裁剪为恰好包围最大矩形的最小边界框。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要完成两层推理——第一层是识别出所有矩形需要按面积排序后嵌套组装（而非保持原位），第二层是发现锚点不是网格中心也不是最大矩形的中心，而是最小矩形的原始位置决定了整个组装结构在输出中的定位。最终输出被裁剪到最大矩形的边界。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/6cbe9eb8, train/22208ba4, eval/2d0172a1, train/57edb29d, train/d749d46f, eval/a6f40cea, train/652646ff, train/4df5b0ae\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6cbe9eb8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4533\nmechanism=0.5568\nlexical=0.0136\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:frame, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:crop_resize, operation:sort_order, output:crop, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6cbe9eb8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.\n\nInput structure\n- A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.\n- The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.\n- A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.\n\nRule\n- Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.\n- Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.\n- Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.\n\nKey insight\n- The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"foreground rectangular frames and solid rectangles over periodic wallpaper\",\n  \"dst\": \"nested lower-left inside the largest foreground rectangle\",\n  \"transform\": \"discard the wallpaper; sort rectangles by bbox area descending; rebuild each frame or solid rectangle, placing each next smaller rectangle at the lower-left of the current frame interior or solid bbox\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to the largest foreground rectangle bbox\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"22208ba4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4221\nmechanism=0.5109\nlexical=0.0135\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:adjacent, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/22208ba4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/22208ba4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the repeated boundary color's rectangles one block inward while leaving singleton boundary rectangles in place.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the most common color.\n- Foreground objects are solid monochrome rectangles touching a grid corner.\n- Exactly one foreground color appears as multiple separate 4-connected objects; other colors appear once.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the multiple objects of the repeated color from their original positions.\n- For each cleared rectangle, translate it away from the row and column border it touches by exactly its height and width.\n- Keep singleton-color objects unchanged; overlapping translated rectangles of the same color merge.\n\nKey insight:\n- Multiplicity selects the moving color, and each boundary rectangle's touched edges determine its inward diagonal translation.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"the foreground color with multiple 4-connected solid rectangles on grid corners\",\n  \"path\": \"from each rectangle's corner, move inward away from the touched row and column borders by one rectangle height/width\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"translate each selected rectangle once; same-color overlaps merge\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear selected rectangles at their original positions; leave singleton-color rectangles unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2d0172a1\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4018\nmechanism=0.4989\nlexical=0.0131\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:frame, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:crop_resize, operation:sort_order, output:crop, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/2d0172a1.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2d0172a1.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nConvert a rough nested line drawing into a clean canonical frame-and-dot diagram.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\n- Foreground 4-connected objects are rough closed frames or small filled blobs.\n- Frames may contain other frames/blobs; blobs outside a frame remain outside it.\n\nRule:\n- Detect the containment tree of foreground objects using holes of each frame object.\n- Replace every blob with one foreground pixel.\n- Replace every frame with a rectangular border padded two cells around its direct children.\n- Place siblings by their original row/column overlap and order, with one empty cell between canonical objects.\n\nKey insight: The exact wobbly geometry is irrelevant; only enclosure plus relative sibling positions define the output.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"rough two-color nested foreground drawing: closed frame objects and small blob objects\",\n  \"dst\": \"canonical frame-and-dot diagram preserving containment and sibling row/column order\",\n  \"transform\": \"replace each blob by one pixel; replace each frame by a rectangular border padded around its direct children; keep outside blobs outside the enclosing frame\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"canonical crop; root-level outside blobs occupy a 3x3 bg slot\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"57edb29d\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3977\nmechanism=0.4398\nlexical=0.0135\ncode_feature=0.8000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:output_resize, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:crop_resize, operation:sort_order, output:crop, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/57edb29d.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/57edb29d.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExtract the single plain rectangle and redraw it with the aligned rectangles' border-relative marker pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- The boundary color is the background/separator.\n- Foreground objects are dense rectangular regions; exactly one rectangle has only its base color.\n- Other rectangles contain their base color plus marker pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Crop the only plain rectangle; this crop is the output canvas.\n- Use marked rectangles whose row span overlaps the plain rectangle's row span.\n- Transfer their marker pixels by preserving each marker run's distance from the nearest rectangle edges.\n\nKey insight:\n- The marked rectangles are examples of an edge-relative pattern, so the missing plain rectangle receives the same pattern resized to its own dimensions.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"edge-relative marker run s in a marked rectangle aligned with the plain rectangle row band\",\n  \"dst\": \"run d in the plain rectangle crop\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.nearest_edge_offsets == d.nearest_edge_offsets\",\n  \"transform\": \"paint each matched d with the shared marker color; keep base rectangle fill elsewhere\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"same shape as the plain rectangle\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d749d46f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4111\nmechanism=0.4948\nlexical=0.0134\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/d749d46f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPack each solid foreground rectangle twice: wide across the top and tall from the bottom.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has one background color and one foreground color; the foreground forms\nseparate solid rectangles, ordered from left to right.\n\nRule\nBuild a 10-row background canvas whose width is the packed width 